children.translated_text:
Those with yellow hair, with green hair, with tawny hair, and likewise
those with white hair, those with serpent-[like] hair, those without hair;
those with matted heads, with ugly heads, the extremely stout, the flat-nosed;
those with donkey or pig heads, two-headed, or headless;
those with elephant ears, horse ears, rhinoceros-monkey ears;
those with donkey or pig ears, one-eared, or earless;
those with red eyes, bulging eyes, sunken eyes, excessively tawny-eyed;
those with glass eyes, bubble eyes, one-eyed, or eyeless;
those with elephant noses, horse noses, rhinoceros-monkey noses;
those with donkey or pig noses, one-nosed, or noseless;
those with elephant lips, horse lips, rhinoceros-monkey lips;
those with donkey or pig lips, one-lipped, or lipless;
those with elephant teeth, horse teeth, rhinoceros-monkey teeth;
those with donkey or pig teeth, one-toothed, or toothless;
those with overly long necks, those without necks, those with shoulder-eyes, and the hunchbacked;
those with tails severed, with wind-swollen testicles, one-testicled, or without testicles;
the overly tall, the overly short, the emaciated, and those severely afflicted with skin disease;
and those of the four skin colors, the deformed and the misshapen —
one should consider the rejection of such persons as well.
